  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/magic/perception/eye-ringed-glow-angry-small-teal.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Champions Guild Automation:</em> <strong>Additional Spells:</strong> Detect Evil and Good, Mind Spike, Clairvoyance, Divination and Scrying are always prepared once you have slots of that level (add them from the compendium). <strong>Prescient Intervention:</strong> when a creature within 60 ft makes a D20 Test, your Reaction gives it Advantage or Disadvantage. The module offers it when it can change the result: an ally's failed save or missed attack (Advantage), or an enemy's hit on you or an ally, or its successful save against you or an ally (Disadvantage) - it rolls the second d20. Once per Long Rest (the feat's use); casting a Divination spell with a slot gives the use back. Use the activity for ability checks by hand.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
